Syeda Salsabil Islam received the B.Sc. degree in Electrical and Electronic Engineering from Leading University, Sylhet, Bangladesh. She served as the Chairperson of the IEEE Leading University Student Branch, where she was actively involved in technical, academic, and professional activities. Her research interests include power electronics, DC–DC converters, intelligent control systems, machine learning, deep learning, embedded systems, and renewable energy systems. Her research focuses on the development and application of intelligent control techniques for power electronic converter systems.

